    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d267">

                <pb facs="0407" n="291" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg291"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.00/1723.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Johnson to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Santo Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-07-26T15:00:00-04:40">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 26, 1915—3 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Nashville</hi> arrived 23d. Country quiet on the surface
                    except Macoris and La Romana. News just received that rebels took latter town
                    yesterday sacking it and destroying customhouse records and left going towards
                    Macoris. Government has despatched more troops but preferred <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Nashville</hi> to remain here where Government sees
                    possibilities of trouble.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
